{
  "id": "ss.terrain.saltplate",
  "name": "Salt plate",
  "description": "Salt Pan set dressing, and the one cover the pan gives: a plate of salt crust heaved up on its edge, a faceted slab lit hard from above — bone-white crown, husk-coloured face, an ink underside where it left the ground — with two cracks across it and grit at its foot. Blocking, radius 16; drawn round-ish so the game's circle capsule fits it. Deliberately angular against everything else on the ground, which is all curves: a plate is the only straight edge on the pan, and a straight edge is what a shot stops at. Second pass: the face in shade along its lower right, a pale facet on the crown, a crust of salt white along the crown's upper edges, a lit lip beside each crack, a chip at the foot and the dark where it meets the pan. Its ink under-shape stands about one unit proud of the face, not two: at two it drew the plate twice as heavy as the bodies beside it, and feelers scatters it at up to 1.5x.",
  "tags": ["terrain"],
  "size": [44, 36],
  "meta": {"radius": 16},
